.TH NC 1
.SH NAME
nc \- connect to a TCP or UDP port, or wait for a connection
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nc
.RB [ \-u ]
.I host port
.br
.B nc \-l
.RB [ \-u ]
.I port
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nc
connects to
.I port
of
.I host
(TCP, or UDP with
.BR \-u ):
each line typed goes there, and what comes back is shown. Ctrl-D ends it.
.PP
.B nc
is another name of
.BR fetch (1).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-u
UDP instead of TCP.
.TP
.B \-l
Listen: wait on
.I port
for one connection (with
.BR \-u ,
the lines typed go to the last sender).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR netstat (1),
.BR fetch (1),
.BR netd (4)
.SH BUGS
.B nc
works a line at a time (the console gives typed lines); when the other
side closes, it ends at the next Enter (a console read under way cannot be
taken back). No
.B nc
in a pipe: the shell has no pipes.
